{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry your computer is giving you trouble again. I'd like to help, but I need a bit more detail first so I don't guess wrong. Could you tell me: 1) What exactly happens? For example, is it slow or freezing, crashing, showing a blue screen, not turning on, not connecting to the network, or showing an error message? If there's an error, please send the exact wording or a screenshot. 2) When did it start this time, and roughly when did it happen before? 3) Is this your company laptop (BL-LT-0107)? When did you last fully restart it (Start > Power > Restart, not just closing the lid)? 4) Did it start after an update or after you installed a new app? Also, our records show your laptop hasn't checked in with our management system for about 12 days. Is it powered on and connecting to the network, and do you have it with you? Once I hear back, I'll pick this up right away.",
  "internal_note": "Vague ticket ('doing the thing again'), no symptoms given. User Sofia Rossi (ID 7, Marketing, not VIP). Account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked. One device: BL-LT-0107 (Win11 Pro), currently offline, last check-in 2026-09-27, warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Disk is fine (140 GB free, 54.7%), so low disk space isn't the cause. No earlier ticket history was available to tell what 'the thing' is. I asked for symptoms, error text, restart and update history, and confirmation that the device is working and in her hands. The 12-day missed check-in could mean the laptop won't boot, has network or agent trouble, or, less likely, has been misplaced. If she says it's lost, treat it as P1 under KB-021. If she describes slowness or freezing, follow KB-019. Blue screens or repeated crashes go to Tier 2.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-019"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
